{"name":"Damson Plum","hex":"#dda0dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"damson plum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous tree, Prunus insititia, native to Eurasia and related to the plum.","Syzygium cumini, jambul, native to south Asia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damson_plum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Damson","blocks":[{"text":"The damson, damson plum, or damascene, is an edible drupaceous fruit, a subspecies of the plum tree. Varieties of insititia are found across Europe, but the name damson is derived from and most commonly applied to forms that are native to Great Britain. Damsons are small, ovoid, plum-like fruit with a distinctive, somewhat astringent taste, and are widely used for culinary purposes, particularly in fruit preserves and jams."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Damson_plum_fruit.jpg/330px-Damson_plum_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Damson"},{"title":"Chrysophyllum oliviforme","blocks":[{"text":"Chrysophyllum oliviforme, commonly known as the satinleaf, is a medium-sized tree native to Florida, the Bahamas, the Greater Antilles, and Belize. It is also known as damson plum, wild star-apple and saffron-tree. It gets the name \"satinleaf\" from the distinctive colors of the leaves. The top of the leaf is dark green while the bottom is light brown or copper. This distinctive look makes it a very aesthetically pleasing tree that is commonly used as an ornamental in yards and public spaces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Chrysophyllum_oliviforme_01.jpg/330px-Chrysophyllum_oliviforme_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chrysophyllum_oliviforme"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum"},{"title":"Plum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Plum is a purple color with a brownish-gray tinge, like that shown on the right, or a reddish purple, which is a close representation of the average color of the plum fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Plum_on_tree02.jpg/330px-Plum_on_tree02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cvet_%C5%A1ljive_2.JPG/500px-Cvet_%C5%A1ljive_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cvet_%C5%A1ljive_2.JPG/1280px-Cvet_%C5%A1ljive_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cvet_%C5%A1ljive_2.JPG/500px-Cvet_%C5%A1ljive_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Damson flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACvet_%C5%A1ljive_2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Darwin_Domestic_143.png/500px-Darwin_Domestic_143.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Darwin_Domestic_143.png/500px-Darwin_Domestic_143.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Comparison of plum stones: Shropshire damson shown top row, second from left (no. 2). From Charles Darwin's Variation of Animals and Plants under Domestication","link":"https://en.wik